Depends on: the Git::Raw API card.
Evidence: the rename event is {type, from, to} without `page`; `_fire_on_change` passes `$event->{page}` (Server.pm:600), i.e. undef. `auto_commit` only does `$index->add` (History.pm:211), which fails for a deleted file; a rename needs remove(from) + add(to). bin/mcp-wiki:34 then warns "uninitialized value".

Fix: with use_git, rename_page commits the removal of `from` and the addition of `to`; delete_page commits the removal. The event payloads stay as they are (no new keys).

Tests: without Git::Raw, a stand-in git_history with use_git=>1 records the auto_commit calls per event type (create, update, rename, delete; none for restore). In the opt-in real-Git::Raw file, rename and delete appear in git log and the work tree is clean afterwards.

tests: t/50-git-rename-delete.t (opt-in real Git::Raw, no stand-in). Plain and non-ASCII (sub/älter.md -> sub/日本/neu.md): rename = exactly one new commit, HEAD has to / lacks from, index tree == HEAD tree, every work-tree file equals its HEAD blob, event keys unchanged; delete likewise. Red on HEAD 12 of 31 (no commits for rename/delete, work tree not in HEAD). Delete of a page below a non-ASCII dir is NOT used: delete_page answers 'Page not found' for sub/日本/neu.md even without git (path resolution with non-ASCII dirs, same family as card 16).

